  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-antuta-high-quality-wild-betta-fish-lb",
      "html": "<ul><li>Wild-caught, from Indonesia (\"LB\" location).</li><li>Belongs to the Betta unimaculata complex.</li><li>Maximum size: 5 inches (about 12.7 cm).</li><li>IUCN Red List: not listed (not found on IUCN).</li><li>Breeding: mouthbrooder.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-antuta-high-quality-wild-betta-fish-lb",
      "html": "<p>Imported from Indonesia. This batch is from a location designated as LB.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-antuta-high-quality-wild-betta-fish-lb",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: about 60–100</li><li>pH: 5.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 22–28 °C (72–82 °F); cooler temperatures are preferred, but higher temperatures bring out coloration and breeding behaviour.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-antuta-high-quality-wild-betta-fish-lb",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed on live, frozen and dried foods, such as blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-antuta-high-quality-wild-betta-fish-lb",
      "html": "<p>Like many of the species in this complex, and being among the largest bettas, they can be aggressive. It is recommended to keep them in a species-only tank, as they can eat anything that fits in their big mouth.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-antuta-high-quality-wild-betta-fish-lb",
      "html": "<p>Mouthbrooder.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-antuta-high-quality-wild-betta-fish-lb",
      "html": "<p>Brown base body with blue/green iridescence on the head and body. Best known for the larger dragon-like scales on the head. This location has a nice full blue mask on the head and good body masking.</p>"
    }
  ],
